WEBVTT

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.730
Sorry. That's heavy, isn't it?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.400
You have enough books for a summer vacation research project.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.780
Um...

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.570
By the way...

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.490
What?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.160
My...

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.250
My husband is the only one I...

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.340
He's the only one I ever...

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:34.130
My husband was my first love.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:35.930
I think.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.810
So, uh...

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:47.770
I can say that Shimao is the only person I ever really dated.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.990
And I had a crush on him first...

00:00:54.990 --> 00:01:01.450
So I never thought after getting to this age that someone would have feelings for me.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.250
I'm sorry.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.250
I...

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.720
I...

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.640
love you too, Hazuki.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:32.280
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:38.450
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:45.000
I was prepared for the time you left

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:51.840
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.340
After I embraced you with all I had

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:07.900
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:11.570
filled my heart

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:18.070
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:24.750
You gave me happiness

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.080
Until I meet you again one day

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.580
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.130
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:37.800
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:38.930
I won't forget your smile

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.070
<i>Pointless resistance.</i>

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.780
<i>A vain struggle.</i>

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.410
<i>I knew it from the start.</i>

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.330
<i>In the end, I even borrowed his body.</i>

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.420
<i>What did I want to do?</i>

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.210
<i>My body may've died, but I'm still here.</i>

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.300
<i>It looks like she mustered up courage to confess her feelings,</i>

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.260
<i>but if when I reach for her...</i>

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.730
<i>Look. She's waiting in anticipation.</i>

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.230
<i>But this hand isn't mine.</i>

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.690
Just looking at your face is...

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:37.990
<i>This voice, too.</i>

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.740
<i>Even though I'm right here...</i>

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.250
Hazuki?

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.880
Are you free right now?

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.210
Today, I want to...

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.380
<i>...have you all to myself.</i>

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:05.050
Let me call you Rokka instead of Manager.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.930
What's gotten into you?

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:08.140
Rokka.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.020
After all...

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.930
Before, you didn't like that,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.020
but I think it suits you more.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:15.520
It suits me?

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.690
Just for one day is fine.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.150
Just one day.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.150
Okay.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:24.200
And as long as I'm being selfish,

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.330
I'm gonna take half the day.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:30.330
Let's go somewhere we can get a nice view of the big blue sky.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:45.220
<i>Hey, what the hell is this?</i>

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.890
<i>The scenery suddenly changed.</i>

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.400
<i>Where did Manager Thumbelina go?</i>

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.180
<i>Gimme a break.</i>

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.730
I think I understand.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.730
That's why the prince likes you.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.860
You can't drown in this sea.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.070
Your body is in another place right now.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.130
See? You're fine, right?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.750
This is...

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.300
I mean, we can talk!

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.300
That's right. Everything is fine.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:08.260
What's the story this time?

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.850
I don't know.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:13.220
Um... I don't remember reading this.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.770
This won't continue forever.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.190
It'll only grow sadder if it's drawn out.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:25.360
He should know that better than anyone.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.740
I can see it!

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.450
The sea!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.080
Yeah.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:42.540
I think the last time I suddenly decided to ride the train was when I was a student.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.550
But it's exciting riding once in a while.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.260
Yeah.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:54.260
<i>Right now, it doesn't matter to me who Rokka thinks she's spending time with.</i>

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.810
<i>Though my form may've changed,</i>

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.770
<i>I don't want to</i>

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.900
<i>leave your side for even one step.</i>

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.570
What do you want?

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.780
I want to make Rokka happy.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:10.070
If you really are dead, then it's impossible.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:12.820
<i>Impossible or not, I don't care.</i>

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:18.330
<i>At some point, I gave up on my disease, on having a kid, on the shop, everything.</i>

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.670
<i>Shouldn't I be allowed to</i>

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.550
<i>have at least one thing that I can't give up?</i>

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.390
I'm a little hungry.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:35.350
Want to walk to a shop on the beach or whatever?

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.430
But I'm sure it'll be crowded.

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:40.600
Since we're here already, maybe it'd be nice to get some good food in the area.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.400
I don't know anything about this place, though.

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:44.940
Should I check it out on my cell phone?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.900
You can do that?

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.570
Although it'd be faster to use your smart phone, Hazuki.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.240
Remember, you used it to check out Hanayashiki when we went there.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:57.120
Anyway, what do you wanna eat, Rokka?

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.540
Anything but oysters.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:02.960
That's right, it was a disaster when you went digging for oysters a long time ago, and got sick from them.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:07.340
What?! Did Miho tell you about that too?!

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.800
I'm so embarrassed!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.720
She talks too much, you know?

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.100
How much did you hear?

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:18.520
Oh, I just got the bare bones version, so there's no need to...

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.770
Forget about it.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:20.350
Okay.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.860
<i>I remember when that happened very well.</i>

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.360
Rokka can't come today.

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.610
She was taken to the hospital for food poisoning.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:32.240
What did she eat?

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.030
Oysters.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.610
Is she okay?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.080
Yeah. It looks like she'll just have to be hospitalized for the night.

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:41.830
<i>Unexpectedly, Rokka's absence</i>

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:45.460
<i>made me feel the anxiety that I usually caused her to feel.</i>

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.630
Shoot...

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.300
<i>After you were released,</i>

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.220
<i>you came right over with an embarrassed grin,</i>

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.180
<i>and from that day to my last,</i>

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:00.220
<i>no matter what shape I was in,</i>

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.640
<i>your expression never faltered.</i>

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.270
<i>If you had crumbled while I was within reach,</i>

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.610
<i>I could've lent you her a shoulder to cry on...</i>

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.650
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.360
<i>If I could be been born again,</i>

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:20.740
<i>I'd still want to marry you.</i>

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.670
After all, that's just your husband's ego, isn't it?

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:30.960
Even though he understands the situation better than anyone,

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.800
it doesn't change the fact that he's out of his mind.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.930
I have no idea what he's doing.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.430
I'm surprised you lent your body to someone like that.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.390
Good point.

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:43.060
But, well...

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.150
I was prepared to shoulder the burden for both of them.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.190
I don't know why, though.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:51.190
So you're fond of...

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.480
Of course.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:53.320
...the prince.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.570
Of course not!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.410
You're the one that I...

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:58.780
I see.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.620
You're sexually obsessed with Manager.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.080
You have my condolences.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.080
I thought there would be more people.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.420
Swimming season hasn't started yet.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.590
I see. It's a little early.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.840
I don't care. I don't especially want to swim.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.550
I want to swim when I get warm.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.300
Really?

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.470
When I get warm.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.350
Anyway, I don't see any beach shops here.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:22.720
Yeah, there is.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.220
Look over there.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.850
They're selling fireworks already.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.980
I wonder if it's okay to set them off on the beach here.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.690
Wanna shoot some off later?

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:31.860
Wait here.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:32.730
Hey!

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.290
I've got sand all over.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.830
I gave up already.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.540
Maybe there's a place where we can wash off.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.710
Why not with sea water?

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:54.880
I'd get all sticky.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.130
Then give up.

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.170
It's the beach, after all.

00:10:58.760 --> 00:10:59.680
Yeah...

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.600
I like how quiet the sea is.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.140
That's because tomorrow's a weekday.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.060
It's so quiet, it's scary.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:12.110
Because it's pitch-dark?

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:14.070
I'm even scared of the sound of the waves.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:15.150
It's creepy.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.450
You say that, but you're here with me, watching them.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:19.450
Well, after all...

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:22.160
In fact, you're too amiable, Rokka.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.490
You've been ferried around for half the day.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.540
It's been fun.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.790
What's so good about him?

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:31.790
This guy just has youth going for him.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.290
You're talking about yourself?

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.340
He doesn't have any money or qualifications.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.090
On top of that, he still goes to a public bath, in this day and age.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.130
Why are you suddenly coming down hard on yourself?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.010
I probably shouldn't be saying this,

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.890
but you have lousy taste in men, Rokka.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.140
What's up with all this?

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.560
Do you want me to cheer you up?

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.190
Dunno.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.170
<i>I'm not especially surprised.</i>

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.630
<i>This was inevitable.</i>

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.100
<i>Except for me, maybe all of this was meant to be.</i>

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.020
<i>Pointless resistance.</i>

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:39.780
<i>A vain struggle.</i>

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.400
<i>I knew it from the start.</i>

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:57.280
<i>Even though</i>

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.960
<i>I don't want anyone to take her from me...</i>

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.490
Atsushi
Hazuki
I'll call you this afternoon.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:29.240
This character...
Atsushi
Hazuki
I'll call you this afternoon.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.240
Hazuki

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.710
Why?

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.230
<i>Just like it was then.</i>

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:05.320
<i>Just like it was when I used it back then.</i>

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.820
<i>The desk, the chair, the bookshelf,</i>

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:09.910
<i>even the books.</i>

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:18.710
Rokka,

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.750
you kept all of my things.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.380
How in love with me are you?

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.030
<i>The warmth of another person is scary.</i>

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:51.490
<i>Forgotten loneliness easily thaws out.</i>

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:58.120
<i>And for Hazuki to leave before me without even saying a word...</i>

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.540
<i>I don't understand.</i>

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.920
<i>What is he thinking?</i>

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:06.210
<i>And also...</i>

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.130
Atsushi
Hazuki
I'll call you this afternoon.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:08.970
<i>That telegram-like note...
Atsushi
Hazuki
I'll call you this afternoon.</i>

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:10.390
Atsushi
Hazuki
<i>That telegram-like note...</i>

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:11.470
Hazuki
Atsushi

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.010
<i>It can't be.</i>

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.350
Take... Take, Take...

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.480
It's "takekanmuri".

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:19.690
That character exists?

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.770
Yes!

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:22.980
And someone with an odd name like "Rokka" shouldn't talk.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.360
Hmm... Take... Take!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.280
This character?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.240
With the character for "horse" under it.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.150
Shimao Atsushi.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:31.030
Did you finish?

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:32.160
Yep!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.580
Now I've got a powerful ally who can help me in times of need!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.370
That's an exaggeration.

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:40.870
After all, you know more about soil and fertilizer than anyone in class, Shimao.

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:43.500
You're the King of Horticulture, a real potting soil geek.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:44.630
Is that a compliment?

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.050
Come on, I'm always telling you...

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:51.470
I've been a fan of yours since the pre-admission exhibition.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.640
Though my work didn't even get an honorable mention...

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.180
Even though it was huge and daring,

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.900
at first glance, its creator seems to be the exact opposite.

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.020
Why is that?

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.030
I don't know.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.650
Are you actually vain?

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:15.450
<i>Ever since then, I loved those marble-like eyes that seemed to see right through you.</i>

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.620
<i>Even after my death.</i>

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:21.580
<i>Even though I know that I'm no good for her now.</i>

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:27.590
For that last exhibition, what were those leaves that looked like a gray carpet?

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:28.420
Snow-in-Summer.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:31.010
That was interesting.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.140
It was so cute how the blooming white flowers here and there looked like stars,

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.390
and yet the title was "President Octopus", right?

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.930
I had to laugh at the orange roses that made up its body.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.060
At the time, I didn't have money to buy materials,

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.980
so I chose flowers that seemed okay to use from the flower bed at my house.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:50.400
So that Snow-in-Summer is those gray leaves, huh?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.740
Until now, I've had a different image of them.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:53.660
They're usually mixed in with Meadowsweet.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:54.990
<i>I was hard of hearing in my right ear because of my disease,
They're usually mixed in with Meadowsweet.</i>

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:55.990
<i>I was hard of hearing in my right ear because of my disease,</i>

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.080
So there are different varieties?
<i>I was hard of hearing in my right ear because of my disease,</i>

00:16:57.080 --> 00:17:00.240
They're two totally different things. The rose family and the pink family.
<i>so she always talked softly to me from my left side.</i>

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:00.700
They're two totally different things. The rose family and the pink family.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.630
<i>That voice will never</i>

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.590
<i>call my name again...</i>

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.090
<i>It's only natural that you fell for someone else.</i>

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:17.180
<i>So the only thing</i>

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:22.180
<i>I can do to make you happy with my own hands is...</i>

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.190
<i>Whose desire is this?</i>

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:27.480
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.190
<i>I'm impressed by my own tenacity.</i>

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.740
<i>Should I just call him?</i>

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.990
<i>Or should I wait and see what happens?</i>

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.740
<i>If he doesn't call,</i>

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:46.750
<i>I'd kind of like to avoid suddenly coming face-to-face with him tomorrow at the shop.</i>

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:51.090
<i>I never imagined something like this could happen with a part-time worker.</i>

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:55.630
<i>But when you're alive, you never know what's going to happen.</i>

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.090
<i>I never thought</i>

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:02.270
<i>I'd fall in love with anyone other than Shimao...</i>

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:08.770
<i>I'd better do that, too.</i>

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:22.540
Hey...

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.040
What is this?

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:26.620
How heavy is this Pandora's Box?

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:29.830
Why am I doing this in the first place?

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.590
You started doing it yourself.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.010
Because there isn't anything else to do!

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:37.970
It's not fair there's been absolutely nothing up until now, is it?

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.930
It's because of the author's sudden illness.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.310
More correctly, his sudden death.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.220
What's that?

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.220
Talking about the prince?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.680
Correct.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.810
The prince was vain, but when he was on the verge of death,

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:52.270
he wrote a short letter on the last page of this sketchbook,

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:56.650
then ripped it out and threw it away...

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.990
three times.

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.990
His last words?

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.240
Yes. But,

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:05.240
thinking the reader would just be turned off, he changed his mind, intending to dispose of them.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:08.870
However, after he died, the notes were found when the room was cleaned up,

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.830
which must've been very regrettable.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:17.130
Then just maybe, if I resolve that, the "go to heaven" flag will be raised!

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:24.560
The protagonist of the story does have to become happy, doesn't he?

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:28.390
But just who is the main character of this story?

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.650
<b>By Hans Christian Andersen
Thumbelina
Thumbelina</b>

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:39.200
<i>If I don't hear anything by 2:00, I'm going home.</i>

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.660
Hazuki Ryousuke

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.250
<i>Still,</i>

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:56.170
<i>who would've thought I'd be able to clean up my own mess this way?</i>

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.920
<i>Could it be any more ironic?</i>

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.150
Hazuki, your text came so late!

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.780
You should've called me!

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.160
If you'd told me you were at the shop...

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:06.070
<i>What in the world?</i>

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.040
<i>I have no idea</i>

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.000
<i>which one of them it is...</i>

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:13.960
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:15.710
This is obstruction of someone's business...

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:17.040
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:18.250
President Octopus.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:20.000
COD
<b>For Flower Arrangements
</b>IOU
<b>Hazuki</b>

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:25.380
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:31.140
you always smile

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:35.230
Tell me why

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:39.110
it won't go away

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:40.900
I gave you everything

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.740
You gave me anything

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:47.530
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.200
still my everything

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:52.410
I love you

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:55.790
It is a miracle

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:58.920
like fleeting snow

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:04.880
that fell in summer

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:11.890
If I hadn't met you

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:15.100
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:22.610
and nothing would have pressed down on my chest

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.280
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:35.330
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:40.460
When I close my eyes

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:44.460
you're right beside me
